
@startuml
top to bottom direction

class Program {
    + Main(args : string[]) : void
}


class Scripture {
    - _reference : Reference
    - _words : List<Word>
    - _random : Random

    + Scripture(reference : Reference, text : string)
    + HideRandomWords(numberToHide : int) : void
    + GetDisplayText() : string
    + IsCompletelyHidden() : bool
}



class Reference {
    - _book : string
    - _chapter : int
    - _verse : int
    - _endVerse : int

    + Reference(book : string, chapter : int, verse : int)
    + Reference(book : string, chapter : int, verse : int, endVerse : int)
    + GetDisplayText() : string
}



class Word {
    - _text : string
    - _isHidden : bool

    + Word(text : string)
    + Hide() : void
    + Show() : void
    + IsHidden() : bool
    + GetDisplayText() : string
}


note right of Program
  PROGRAM FLOW
  1. Creates the scripture reference.
  2. Creates the Scripture object.
  3. Displays the scripture.
  4. Prompts Enter or quit.
  5. Hides random words when Enter is pressed.
  6. Ends when the user quits
     or all words are hidden.
end note

Program ..> Scripture : creates and uses


note left of Scripture
  SCRIPTURE CLASS

  ATTRIBUTES
  _reference: Stores the scripture reference.
  _words: Stores individual Word objects.
  _random: Selects random words.

  CONSTRUCTOR
  Receives the reference and scripture text.
  Splits the text into Word objects.

  METHODS
  HideRandomWords(): Hides selected words.
  GetDisplayText(): Displays the scripture.
  IsCompletelyHidden(): Checks whether
  all words have been hidden.
end note


note left of Reference
  REFERENCE CLASS

  ATTRIBUTES
  _book: Stores the book name.
  _chapter: Stores the chapter number.
  _verse: Stores the starting verse.
  _endVerse: Stores the ending verse.

  CONSTRUCTORS
  Reference(book, chapter, verse):
  Creates a single-verse reference.

  Reference(book, chapter, verse, endVerse):
  Creates a verse-range reference.

  METHOD
  GetDisplayText():
  Formats the scripture reference,
  such as John 3:16 or Proverbs 3:5-6.
end note


note right of Word
  WORD CLASS

  ATTRIBUTES
  _text: Stores the original word.
  _isHidden: Tracks whether it is hidden.

  CONSTRUCTOR
  Word(text):
  Initializes the word as visible.

  METHODS
  Hide(): Hides the word.
  Show(): Makes the word visible.
  IsHidden(): Checks its hidden status.
  GetDisplayText(): Returns the word
  or underscores if hidden.
end note


note bottom of Scripture
  HOW THE METHODS WORK TOGETHER

  1. Program.Main() creates a Reference
     and passes it to Scripture().

  2. Scripture() creates Word objects
     from the scripture text.

  3. Program.Main() calls
     Scripture.GetDisplayText()
     to display the scripture.

  4. When Enter is pressed,
     Scripture.HideRandomWords()
     selects words and calls Word.Hide().

  5. Scripture.GetDisplayText() uses
     Reference.GetDisplayText() and
     Word.GetDisplayText() to display
     the updated scripture.

  6. Scripture.IsCompletelyHidden()
     checks Word.IsHidden() to determine
     whether the program should end.
end note




Scripture --> Reference : stores
Scripture "1" --> "1..*" Word : contains

@enduml
